  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/nandus-nebulosus-2/",
      "html": "<p>Usually 4-6 cm long; the largest specimen collected so far was 8 cm. Nandus species do not care for the brood.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/nandus-nebulosus-2/",
      "html": "<p>There are two, pretty similar species of Nandus occurring in Thailand: the deep-bodied N. oxyrhynchus from the basins of the large rivers Mekong and Mae Klong and the somewhat more slender, short-nosed N. nebulosus from the south of the country. However, regions are known where both species occur sympatrically. The greatest part of the natural range of N. nebulosus is the Malay Peninsula and Indonesia.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/nandus-nebulosus-2/",
      "html": "<p>In the wild, N. nebulosus is very often found in blackwater habitats. This type of water is very poor in food, so the tiny size of N. nebulosus is a benefit.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/nandus-nebulosus-2/",
      "html": "<p>Nandus nebulosus looks like an innocent child due to the short snout and the large eyes; the congeneric species look much more \"predatory\". But one should not make the mistake of underestimating N. nebulosus: this fish easily swallows fish of half of its own body size. Besides this, all Nandus species are very peaceful fish.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/nandus-nebulosus-2/",
      "html": "<p>Nandids belonging to the genus Nandus do not take care of the brood, while most other members of the family do.</p>"
    }
  ],
